{"Title":"An Act to ease burdens on litigants \r\n","BillNumber":"H1643","DocketNumber":"HD1797","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J_L1","Name":"Jay D. Livingstone","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/J_L1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T11:58:56.267"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"J_L1","Name":"Jay D. Livingstone","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/J_L1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T11:58:56.2666667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H1643/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Livingstone of Boston, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 1643) of Jay D. Livingstone relative to lowering the age for persons serving certain summonses and complaints.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1: Section 20 of chapter 223 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting the following section: \r\n\t(X) “Notwithstanding any law or rule to the contrary, any person who is at least 18 years old and not a party may serve a summons and complaint for all civil actions pending in District Court, Boston Municipal Court, or Superior Court.”\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}